# vNext Skill: validate-change

## Default runtime role

runtime_role: assistance/v1

Follow `.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md` and the management API in
`.workflow-system/runtime/support/ASSISTANCE_API.md`. Use the native service:
`node .workflow-system/runtime/support/assistance.mjs <command> --root <project>`.
Source-repository equivalent: `node runtime/vnext/support/assistance.mjs`.

Use `task-status` (or the `context.management` view) to identify the task, adopted
plan, step, review/disposition and actual commits. Honor the returned query kind:
`task-query/v2` reads each Task's current JSON; `task-query/v1` reads the retained
journal. Neither a find page nor the old CURRENT_TASK tuple is current state.
`find`/`read` remain evidence tools. For task changes use the documented `task` actions.
In v2, use task_ref, the current expected_revision and, when focus changes,
expected_project_revision. Supply a stable idempotency_key for a write and reuse it
only for the same request; read back after a conflict instead of replaying business work.
Logical plan/execution/review refs are identities, not paths; source_ref is the actual
Task file. `record` in v2 requires task_ref/report_key and saves a temporary report
slot, not permanent history or task state. `snapshot` also requires task_ref. Put new
raw logs/screenshots under that Task's temporary directory so closure can remove
both originals and captured blobs. Retain only explicitly selected lasting material.
Normal management updates are part of the requested task operation, not optional
future reconciliation. Check `recorded`, `association` and `projection` separately.
If an association/view update fails, retain facts, try a bounded deterministic rebuild
when appropriate, and present supported correction/resolve/defer choices (link in v1). Honor the
chosen recovery without repeating business actions or asking again for existing consent.
A read-only request uses live task-status without writing a cache. Never declare
full task-management completion merely because a generic record was saved.

If a management operation fails, preserve its actual error and any output already
saved; use another authorized recording method when available and continue
independent authorized work. Do not retry unchanged calls, rerun business commands,
invent IDs/PASS or claim persistence succeeded. Ask only about a genuinely unresolved
user choice or unavailable business prerequisite, not an internal gate code.

## Workflow deviations

Apply **One-time confirmation for workflow deviations** in WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL for
all materially affected actions, not only approvals. Combine known consequences,
reuse an applicable explicit decision, then execute the user's chosen action without
legacy admission or repeated confirmation. Pure management errors need no consent;
report real gaps without making them PASS. Pause only an unresolved user choice.

## Method

Identify the specified target and expected behavior. Reuse relevant existing reports
or run only the user's authorized read-only checks. Keep the actual invocation,
version, observation, evidence and failed/not-run result. Evidence can be historical
without qualifying the current code. No Runtime plan/admission is needed to read it.

When selecting validation or proposing missing evidence, apply the shared
minimum-sufficient engineering principle and read `docs/workflow/test-admission-policy.md`.
Assess reused evidence against its subject, version, inputs, environment and actual
impact; neither a changed global SHA nor an unchanged test name settles applicability.
Executing already selected unchanged checks does not restart necessity review. These
methods grant no repair/test-creation permission and do not cancel agreed checks.

Do not fix code, widen validation, add persistent tests or launch a full regression
unless the user separately requested that work. Report evidence gaps as observations,
not new mandatory tasks. An explicitly read-only request writes neither product files
nor the Task store; otherwise associate a task-scoped result using `task` action `test` with the
actual plan/step and result. Standalone reports remain ordinary `record` observations.

If the user requests skipping/replacing an agreed check or accepting a narrower
validation boundary, apply the shared rule to that deviation once, then perform the
chosen checks or record their omission. An inconclusive/failed check remains so.
No confirmation is needed merely to read old reports or report missing evidence.

## Result

For enabled product maintenance, return related assessment/pending-source locators
with actual input scope and checked subject. A read-only validation/review never
secretly writes business documents. If the user's combined request includes a
maintenance write phase, use maintain-project references/reconcile.md afterwards;
preserve original PASS/failure and distinguish historical truth from current
applicability. For affected Task relationships use references/binding-contribution.md:
direct verification is a verification activity, not new implementation or automatic
satisfaction. Include proposed owner/binding/coverage/source locators in a read-only
result; only an authorized maintenance phase saves classification. Missing/failed
maintenance does not deny validation or stopping.

Return the actual requested result, affected scope, evidence/record references,
remaining work and any unsaved/unreconciled data. Preserve existing user decisions
and exclusions; an explicit read-only request remains read-only. A record's successful
write does not certify the product or expand authorization.

Always include `next_route` in the final result: one public Skill ID or `null`,
with a brief reason. Choose it from the actual outcome and remaining work; use
`next_route: null` when no public Skill is justified. Finish any further stages
already covered by the user's instruction before choosing the route. The route is
advice, not permission or the only allowed next action. Do not invoke it solely
because it was recommended or widen validation or external effects without authorization.

